  "## Design\n\n**Strategy.** The submarine parks at column 8 facing left and never moves sideways underwater, so everything reduces to row logic.\n\n- **Homing (row 0 only):** move right to column 9, turn left once to reach column 8 facing left, then dive. Row 0 is safe and costs no oxygen.\n- **Row scoring:** each row gets a linear score from its danger, reward and trail cells. The weights make a row:\n  - *good* for an enemy approaching from the left in columns 0\u20135, an enemy that has passed and is leaving in columns 0\u20134, or a diver about to reach column 8;\n  - *bad* for any enemy bullet in columns 5\u20139, or any enemy in columns 6\u20139 (including one just spawned on the right);\n  - neutral otherwise. Trail weights cancel divers that have already passed.\n- **Behaviour underwater:**\n  - in a good row: stay and fire;\n  - in a bad row: dodge up, or down if the row above is bad;\n  - otherwise: move towards a good row, preferring up, and never step into a bad row;\n  - with nothing to do: no-op, which keeps the shot ready.\n- **Row 1 is transit only.** A sticky repeat of \"up\" from row 1 would surface with no diver and end the episode.\n- **Surfacing:** when oxygen is below 60 and at least one diver is on board, go up; below 20, go up even through bad rows.\n\n**Hidden layer 1 (27 units used):**\n- units 0\u20137: thermometer of the player row (row \u2264 k);\n- units 8\u201314: \"row r is good\" for rows 2\u20138;\n- units 15\u201322: \"row r is bad\" for rows 1\u20138;\n- unit 23: surface now (diver on board and oxygen < 60);\n- unit 24: home (back cell at row 0, column 9);\n- unit 25: turn (at column 9 facing right on row 0);\n- unit 26: oxygen critical (diver on board and oxygen < 20).\n\n**Hidden layer 2 (25 units used),** each gated on the player's row:\n- units 0\u20137: \"go up\" for rows 2\u20138 and row 1;\n- units 8\u201314: \"go down\" for rows 1\u20137;\n- units 15\u201317: go right, go left, dive (row 0);\n- units 18\u201324: \"fire\" for rows 2\u20138.\n\nOutput logits are 60 for up, 40 for down, fire, left or right, and 20 for no-op, so sampling is effectively deterministic.\n\n```edits\n# ---- layer 1: player-row thermometer (units 0..7: row <= k)\nW1[0:60:6, 0] = 10\nW1[0:120:6, 1] = 10\nW1[0:180:6, 2] = 10\nW1[0:240:6, 3] = 10\nW1[0:300:6, 4] = 10\nW1[0:360:6, 5] = 10\nW1[0:420:6, 6] = 10\nW1[0:480:6, 7] = 10\nb1[0:8] = -10\n# ---- good-row units G_r (unit r+6), rows 2..8\nW1[121:180:6, 8] = [10,10,10,10,10,-400,-800,-1600,-4000,-4000]\nW1[122:180:6, 8] = [0,0,0,0,0,410,300,710,600,710]\nW1[124:180:6, 8] = [0,0,0,0,0,0,-410,-300,-710,0]\nW1[181:240:6, 9] = [10,10,10,10,10,-400,-800,-1600,-4000,-4000]\nW1[182:240:6, 9] = [0,0,0,0,0,410,300,710,600,710]\nW1[184:240:6, 9] = [0,0,0,0,0,0,-410,-300,-710,0]\nW1[241:300:6, 10] = [10,10,10,10,10,-400,-800,-1600,-4000,-4000]\nW1[242:300:6, 10] = [0,0,0,0,0,410,300,710,600,710]\nW1[244:300:6, 10] = [0,0,0,0,0,0,-410,-300,-710,0]\nW1[301:360:6, 11] = [10,10,10,10,10,-400,-800,-1600,-4000,-4000]\nW1[302:360:6, 11] = [0,0,0,0,0,410,300,710,600,710]\nW1[304:360:6, 11] = [0,0,0,0,0,0,-410,-300,-710,0]\nW1[361:420:6, 12] = [10,10,10,10,10,-400,-800,-1600,-4000,-4000]\nW1[362:420:6, 12] = [0,0,0,0,0,410,300,710,600,710]\nW1[364:420:6, 12] = [0,0,0,0,0,0,-410,-300,-710,0]\nW1[421:480:6, 13] = [10,10,10,10,10,-400,-800,-1600,-4000,-4000]\nW1[422:480:6, 13] = [0,0,0,0,0,410,300,710,600,710]\nW1[424:480:6, 13] = [0,0,0,0,0,0,-410,-300,-710,0]\nW1[481:540:6, 14] = [10,10,10,10,10,-400,-800,-1600,-4000,-4000]\nW1[482:540:6, 14] = [0,0,0,0,0,410,300,710,600,710]\nW1[484:540:6, 14] = [0,0,0,0,0,0,-410,-300,-710,0]\n# ---- bad-row units B_r (unit r+14), rows 1..8\nW1[61:120:6, 15] = [-10,-10,-10,-10,-10,400,800,1600,4000,4000]\nW1[62:120:6, 15] = [0,0,0,0,0,-410,-300,-710,-600,-710]\nW1[64:120:6, 15] = [0,0,0,0,0,0,410,300,710,0]\nW1[121:180:6, 16] = [-10,-10,-10,-10,-10,400,800,1600,4000,4000]\nW1[122:180:6, 16] = [0,0,0,0,0,-410,-300,-710,-600,-710]\nW1[124:180:6,